From 103e52058b63797c9a1ca6e0448f98993827f25c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:23:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 50/52] LuaPlus call helpers restore the stack top by any path

lua_call raises script errors as C++ exceptions (fba488d1), so the 84 LuaFunction helpers' trailing lua_settop
never ran after one: every script error left its message on the stack. A game with ~1,500 OnIntelChange errors
drove the sim's Lua stack past the 2048-slot API limit, after which lua_checkstack failed for everyone (the
agent bridge rejected every reply as 'JSON nested too deeply' from mid-game on). LuaStackTopGuard (RAII, the
lua_State twin of LuaAutoBlock) replaces the saved top in every helper.

Also: LuaPush of a bool accepts exactly bool. A pointer whose class is incomplete at the call matched none of
the object rules and converted to bool, so the script got 'true' in place of the object; that is a compile
error now (include the class's header at the call). nullptr pushes nil.

Ported onto 8977bb9d.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 283fcf568aefaaf96d52ac87503953026fe2d047)

Ported onto 13ce9e55: the original commit had re-saved the whole header with CRLF line endings; only its content change is applied here, keeping the repository's LF.
